// PARAM: --analysis sign
// Sign's Zero element refuting 0 < y, and the same source condition landing
// on two different verdicts at two nodes of one program. The refutation
// route here is Zero, not Negative: sign_lt reaches 0 < y through a
// different case than 02-straight_line_sign_refuted.vimp's exact negative
// write does, and the two-element lattice gap between them (Positive proves,
// Zero refutes) is what an over-eager "any non-Positive is undecided"
// regression would collapse.
//
// The intervening y := 0 is also what keeps the two check nodes from being
// answered by one shared reading: a report that forwarded either node's
// store to the other would have to give both the same verdict.
void main() {
  int32 y;
  y := 5;
  __voblint_check(0 < y); // PROVED
  y := 0;
  __voblint_check(0 < y) // REFUTED
}
